            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0376" n="62" xml:id="pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/439</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-07T15:00:00+02:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 16, 6 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Turkish Cabinet divided. Minister[s] of Marine and Finance favor France; Minister
                    of War influenced by German military commission favors alliance with Germany.
                    Sentiment developing in favor of an invasion of the Caucasus. Minister of the
                    Interior counsels moderation and neutrality. It is feared that Turkey, taking
                    advantage of general conditions, may abrogate capitulations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgenthau</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
